+# Wave 04 · Director coordination and review
+
+Revision 1. The foundation admission is the exact Wave 03 patch on published PI02-P1 `2f90256a1047b748bf99f7aec39b70b2ed1aeffe`. The local `integration/dl-f01-p1` checkpoint contains the approved 16 files. Candidate tooling remains separate from the foundation and has no production entry point.
+
+## Development scenario chooser
+
+Enter from the isolated candidate using existing project dependencies and Playwright.
+
+```powershell
+node BLOB_BOT_SERIES1/director/handoff.mjs <new-external-evidence-directory>
+```
+
+Select a Shelf layout, then Load for human input, Reset for a new disposable context, or Automate and record for the accepted Shelf tape. Setup uses the existing authored patch and development mount. Start verification gates transfer. In the game, Take over requests a native neutral input step. Keep physical controls neutral until the toolbar reports Human input active. Scenario selection closes the game context. The chooser lives outside normal player UI. Closing it exits.
+
+The `--verify` mode checks Load, Reset, automation and takeover, then confirms production keyboard movement after transfer. The frame observer taps the native rendered scene. An optional detail crop narrows the recorded canvas region around the Shelf at the same camera pose. The audio tap reads the existing post-compressor mix and leaves its output path and gain intact. The decoder binds simulation substeps to actual encoded presentation timestamps via the frame code. It reports missing markers and alignment differences without changing time. Media codec availability depends on the browser.
+
+## Comparative library
+
+```powershell
+node BLOB_BOT_SERIES1/director/experiment-library.mjs <new-external-evidence-directory>
+```
+
+One loadable definition pins the exact fixture hash and 1/60-second mounted comparison inputs. It covers ordinary tether Pulse, directed launch and Garden placement, two boosted mobility protocols and three native Pulse bursts per layout. Read the separate accepted telemetry and review report before drawing player-experience conclusions from the unrendered fixture. Neither fixture-only results nor frame-code alignment substitutes for controller acceptance.
+
+## Dependencies and protection
+
+The PI03 audit gates further contact work on a free-material recipient contract. Core support, held Garden contact and crown Flow each have explicit, distinct scopes. PS02/NV02 remain audit contracts with transient input and mount identity reset boundaries. Existing movement, camera, controllers, physiology, ecology, receipt ownership, audio mix and scheduler remain authoritative. LS1E1 and LS1E2 remain baseline exceptions. Foundation promotion is local only. No trade merge or remote publication is part of this coordination record.
